<div class="think-story" aria-label="How the THINK bottleneck changes with AI and Poesis">
  <div class="think-story__phases">
    <article class="think-phase" aria-labelledby="think-history-title">
      <header>
        <span class="think-phase__number">01 · Historically</span>
        <h3 id="think-history-title">THINK stayed implicit and human-bound.</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="think-phase__flow">
        <div class="think-capacity think-capacity--narrow">
          <strong>THINK</strong>
          <span>Implicit · manual · human-held</span>
        </div>
        <span class="think-phase__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="think-capacity-group">
          <div class="think-capacity"><strong>BUILD</strong></div>
          <div class="think-capacity"><strong>RUN</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>BUILD and RUN adapted to the throughput of manual THINK.</p>
      <ul class="think-phase__details">
        <li>Purpose, rules, and constraints lived across people, meetings, documents, and tools.</li>
        <li>Each handoff reconstructed THINK through clarification, coordination, review, and correction.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="think-phase think-phase--warning" aria-labelledby="think-ai-title">
      <header>
        <span class="think-phase__number">02 · AI in BUILD + RUN</span>
        <h3 id="think-ai-title">The old bottleneck becomes unacceptable.</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="think-phase__flow">
        <div class="think-capacity think-capacity--narrow">
          <strong>THINK</strong>
          <span>Same capacity</span>
        </div>
        <span class="think-phase__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="think-capacity-group think-capacity-group--expanded">
          <div class="think-capacity"><strong>AI-ACCELERATED BUILD</strong></div>
          <div class="think-capacity"><strong>AI-ACCELERATED RUN</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>The old bottleneck resurfaces inside BUILD as human harnessing: prompts, reviews, corrections, and controls consume the expected gain.</p>
      <ul class="think-phase__details">
        <li>AI increases the volume and speed of BUILD and RUN without increasing shared THINK.</li>
        <li>People spend the gain restoring intent, checking assumptions, and containing drift and risk.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="think-phase think-phase--poesis" aria-labelledby="think-poesis-title">
      <header>
        <span class="think-phase__number">03 · Poesis</span>
        <h3 id="think-poesis-title">Apply human + AI capacity to THINK first.</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="think-phase__flow">
        <div class="think-capacity think-capacity--governed">
          <strong>GOVERNED THINK</strong>
          <span>Explicit · reusable · machine-operable</span>
        </div>
        <span class="think-phase__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="think-capacity-group think-capacity-group--expanded">
          <div class="think-capacity"><strong>AI-ACCELERATED BUILD</strong></div>
          <div class="think-capacity"><strong>AI-ACCELERATED RUN</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>People retain authority while AI helps make THINK governed, reusable, and shared by BUILD and RUN.</p>
      <ul class="think-phase__details">
        <li>AI sources and structures intent and RUN evidence upstream, where THINK is formed.</li>
        <li>Human-governed definitions become the shared reference for faster BUILD and RUN.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="think-story__consequences" aria-label="Consequences of governed THINK">
    <div class="think-consequence-group">
      <span>Immediate effects</span>
      <strong>More BUILD + RUN throughput</strong>
      <strong>Resource economy</strong>
      <strong>AI governance by design</strong>
    </div>
    <b class="think-consequence-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</b>
    <div class="think-consequence-group think-consequence-group--horizon">
      <span>Three views of one model</span>
      <strong>Executable organizational twin</strong>
      <strong>Organization as a Service (OaaS)</strong>
      <strong>Product as a Service (ProdaaS)</strong>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>